What is DevOps?

DevOps is a culture, a set of practices, and a collection of tools that bring Development (Dev) and Operations (Ops) teams together to deliver software faster, more reliably, and with higher quality through automation and collaboration.

Interview Definition (2 lines):

DevOps is a culture that combines development and operations to automate the software delivery lifecycle, enabling faster, reliable, and continuous delivery of applications.

Why was DevOps Introduced?
