Real-World Example
Without DevOps

A company releases a banking application.

Developers finish coding in January.
Testing completes in February.
Operations deploy in March.
Deployment fails due to missing configurations.
Release is delayed.

Total time: 3 months

With DevOps
Developers push code to GitHub.
CI pipeline builds and tests automatically.
Docker image is created.
Image is scanned for vulnerabilities.
Image is pushed to Azure Container Registry (ACR).
Deployment to AKS happens automatically.
Monitoring starts immediately.
Alerts are generated if issues occur.

Release time: 15–30 minutes (depending on the application)

